---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import SalarioLiquidoCalc from "../../components/SalarioLiquidoCalc.tsx";
---
<Layout
  bleed
  lang="en"
  title="Brazil net salary calculator 2026 (CLT) | Baitaan"
  description="Work out your 2026 net salary in Brazil with the INSS and income tax tables and the new income tax exemption up to R$ 5,000 (Law 15.270/2025). Free, no sign-up."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="Net salary calculator 2026 (Brazil)"
    lead="Since January 2026, people earning up to R$ 5,000 a month pay no income tax at source in Brazil. The INSS social security deduction still applies, from 7.5% to 14% by bracket."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
    sourcesHeading="Sources"
    sources={[
      { href: "https://www.planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2023-2026/2025/lei/L15270.htm", label: "Law 15.270/2025 (income tax reduction)" },
      { href: "https://www.gov.br/inss/", label: "INSS: 2026 contribution table" },
    ]}
  >
    <SalarioLiquidoCalc client:load lang="en" />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>How to calculate net salary</h2>
      <p>Net salary = gross salary − INSS − income tax − other deductions. INSS is calculated bracket by bracket. Income tax is calculated on gross pay minus INSS and dependents (or the simplified deduction of R$ 607.20, whichever is higher).</p>

      <h2>2026 examples</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>R$ 5,000: INSS R$ 501.51, no income tax, net R$ 4,498.49.</li>
        <li>R$ 6,000: INSS R$ 641.51, income tax R$ 385.10 after the reduction, net R$ 4,973.39.</li>
      </ul>

      <AdSlot unit="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <h2>Earning between R$ 5,000 and R$ 7,350</h2>
      <p>In this range the tax isn't zero, but it is lower. The reduction is R$ 978.62 minus 13.3145% of the salary. Above R$ 7,350 the normal table applies.</p>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Is pay up to R$ 5,000 free of income tax in 2026?</summary><p>Yes. Under Law 15.270/2025, the reduction brings the tax to zero for taxable income up to R$ 5,000 a month. On a R$ 5,000 salary, for example, the table gives R$ 312.89 of income tax and the reduction takes off exactly that: net pay is R$ 4,498.49.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>What is the simplified discount?</summary><p>A flat R$ 607.20 a month that replaces the legal deductions (INSS, dependents and alimony). The calculator uses whichever is better for you.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>How much does each dependent reduce?</summary><p>R$ 189.59 a month off the income tax base. For pay up to R$ 5,000 it changes nothing, because the tax is already zero.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Does the exemption also apply to the 13th and holiday pay?</summary><p>Yes, the reduction also applies to income tax on the 13th salary and on holiday pay. See the <a class="text-link underline" href="/en/calculadora-13-salario/">13th salary calculator</a>.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Why doesn't my payslip match exactly?</summary><p>Besides INSS and income tax, a payslip may include transport vouchers (up to 6% of salary), health plan, meal vouchers, absences, overtime or an advance. Enter those in other deductions to check.</p></details>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
